Windows Workflow Foundation 3
-----------------------------

This product includes software from the .NET Framework 4.8 Reference Source
(https://github.com/microsoft/referencesource, commit ec9fa9a), licensed under the MIT License, Copyright (c) Microsoft
Corporation: System.Workflow.ComponentModel/, System.Workflow.Runtime/ and System.Workflow.Activities/, and
System.Messaging/System/Messaging/MessageQueueErrorCode.cs, which System.Workflow.Runtime compiles in.

It is in the external/referencesource submodule (https://github.com/xforcore/referencesource, branch
workflowforcore), compiled by src/workflowForCore.System.Workflow.*; each file keeps its original header, and every
change is a commit on that branch. The assemblies carry Microsoft's public key (token 31bf3856ad364e35,
keys/35MSSharedLib1024.snk, which holds only the public key) so that references to them resolve; they are delay
signed, not signed by Microsoft.

.NET Framework 4.8 data
-----------------------

The Reference Source doesn't include WF3's string resources or the SQL scripts of its persistence and tracking
services. workflowForCore reads them from .NET Framework 4.8 as data, Copyright (c) Microsoft Corporation:
- the string resources (src/*/FrameworkData/*.resx), from the assemblies of Microsoft's reference assemblies package
  for .NET Framework 4.8 (Microsoft.NETFramework.ReferenceAssemblies.net48, MIT License), and checked against .NET
  Framework 4.8's GAC by CI (tools/framework_data.cs);
- the names and defaults of the appSettings keys and AppContext switches WF3 reads (src/FrameworkData/settings.txt,
  tools/framework_settings.cs);
- the SQL scripts of SqlWorkflowPersistenceService and SqlTrackingService
  (src/workflowForCore.System.Workflow.Runtime/FrameworkData/Sql), from .NET Framework 4.8's folder.
No code or IL is copied.

